---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — The Fuel Pulse" description="Who we are, how we collect fuel price data, and why The Fuel Pulse is Latvia's most up-to-date fuel price tracker.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6" data-reveal>

    <div>
      <a href="/" class="text-xs text-base-content/40 hover:text-primary transition-colors mb-3 inline-block">← Back to dashboard</a>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-2">About The Fuel Pulse</h1>
      <p class="text-base-content/60 leading-relaxed">
        Real-time diesel, petrol 95, and petrol 98 prices across Latvia's major fuel networks — updated automatically, three times a day.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 p-6 md:p-8 space-y-8">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">What We Do</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed mb-3">
          The Fuel Pulse tracks retail fuel prices at the pump across Latvia's four major fuel station chains —
          <strong>Circle K</strong>, <strong>Virši</strong>, <strong>Neste</strong>, and <strong>Girteka / Oksana</strong>.
          Prices are scraped directly from each retailer's public pricing pages and aggregated into a single dashboard.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
          On top of raw prices, our AI analysis layer (powered by Google Gemini) reviews current global oil market news
          and issues a daily fill-up recommendation — <em>buy now</em>, <em>wait</em>, or <em>monitor</em> — with a
          plain-language explanation of the key price drivers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Sources &amp; Methodology</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-base-content/30 shrink-0 mt-1">›</span><span><strong>Station prices</strong> — scraped directly from each retailer's public-facing website, three times daily (08:00, 14:00, 20:00 Riga time).</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-base-content/30 shrink-0 mt-1">›</span><span><strong>Market news</strong> — aggregated from Google News RSS feeds filtered for Latvian and Baltic fuel market stories.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-base-content/30 shrink-0 mt-1">›</span><span><strong>Historical data</strong> — stored as daily averages, enabling trend charts going back months.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-base-content/30 shrink-0 mt-1">›</span><span><strong>AI recommendation</strong> — generated by Google Gemini, which reads today's news headlines alongside current station prices to assess short-term price direction.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 mt-3">
          Prices reflect the rates publicly posted by each retailer and may differ slightly from the price you see at the pump due to local promotions or card discounts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Update Frequency</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
          Price data, market news, and AI recommendations are refreshed automatically at <strong>08:00, 14:00, and 20:00 Riga time</strong> every day via a scheduled GitHub Actions pipeline. The timestamp shown on the dashboard always reflects the last completed data run.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Why Trust This Data?</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed mb-3">
          Unlike manually-maintained price comparison sites, The Fuel Pulse has no human editorial step between the retailer's website and what you see on screen. Our scraper reads prices from the same URLs you would visit yourself — there is no rounding, no delay, and no incentive to misrepresent figures.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
          Every data point is timestamped and the full price history is stored, so you can see exactly when prices changed and by how much. The AI recommendation clearly states its confidence level and cites the news sources it used — you are never asked to trust a black box.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed mb-2">
          Questions, data corrections, or partnership enquiries:
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:info@thefuelpulse.com" class="link link-primary">info@thefuelpulse.com</a>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 leading-relaxed">
          The Fuel Pulse provides publicly available pricing data for informational purposes only. We are not affiliated with any fuel retailer. Prices may vary by station location, loyalty programme, or payment method. We accept no liability for decisions made based on information presented on this site.
          The AI fill-up recommendation is an automated analysis of market trends and does not constitute financial advice.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
